{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "6f63ca78-4cef-5d96-9c3d-257f6e6b0fc8",
    "name": "Ch29 Team Workflow",
    "description": "# Ch29 Team Workflow\n\nA small shared smoke suite that follows team rules:\n\n- **No secrets in the collection.** Usernames and passwords come from the environment (`username`, `password`). In CI they are passed with `--env-var`.\n- **Runtime values stay in collection variables** (`token`, `orderId`), so they never leak into a shared environment.\n- **Every change goes through a fork and a pull request** (or a Git branch and a pull request).\n\nRun: `newman run collections/ch29-team-workflow.postman_collection.json -e collections/local.postman_environment.json`",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Smoke",
      "description": "Three quick checks that run first in every pipeline: is the API up, can we log in, does the token work.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('API is up', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('UP');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Log in (credentials from the environment)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Login works with the environment credentials', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "// keep the token in a collection variable: it is a runtime value, not config",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', pm.response.json().token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Who am I",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('The token belongs to the configured user', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().username).to.eql(pm.environment.get('username'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "AI draft review",
      "description": "The same request with a first-draft test (the kind an AI assistant often proposes) and with a reviewed test. Compare what each one would catch.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Place an order: first draft test",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 201\", function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test(\"Response has id\", function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.have.property(\"id\");",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('orderId', pm.response.json().id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/orders",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "orders"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"productId\": 1,\n  \"quantity\": 2\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Cancel the first order (cleanup)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Order cancelled', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "orders",
                "{{orderId}}"
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Place an order: reviewed test",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const order = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('201 Created with a Location header for the new order', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.header('Location', '/api/orders/' + order.id);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Order has what we sent, is PLACED and belongs to us', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(order).to.include({ productId: 1, quantity: 2, status: 'PLACED' });",
                  "  pm.expect(order.owner).to.eql(pm.environment.get('username'));",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Total = price x quantity (price read from the API)', (done) => {",
                  "  const url = pm.environment.get('baseUrl') + '/api/products/1';",
                  "  pm.sendRequest(url, (err, res) => {",
                  "    pm.expect(err).to.eql(null);",
                  "    pm.expect(order.total).to.eql(res.json().price * 2);",
                  "    done();",
                  "  });",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('orderId', order.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/orders",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "orders"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"productId\": 1,\n  \"quantity\": 2\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Cancel the reviewed order (cleanup)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Order cancelled', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "orders",
                "{{orderId}}"
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Vault demo",
      "description": "Works in the Postman app after you add a vault secret named `qa-api-key` (value `qa-key-123`). **Fails in Newman on purpose:** Newman cannot read your vault, so it sends the text `{{vault:qa-api-key}}` and gets 401.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Sales report with the vault key",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('The vault secret was sent as the API key', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "x-api-key",
                "value": "{{vault:qa-api-key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/reports/sales",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "reports",
                "sales"
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "orderId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ]
}
